**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Food Delivery in a Hospital**

| **Name** | **Text** | **Runtime** | **Goal Type** | **Relation** | **Justification** |
|----------|----------|-------------|---------------|--------------|--------------------|
| **G1: Deliver Food from Kitchen to Inpatient Room** | Execute the complete food‑delivery operation – pick up meals, transport them and hand them to the patient or place them on the bedside table. | `;` (sequential) | Perform | AND (to G2 & G3) | The operation must first acquire the meal(s) in the kitchen and only then proceed to the delivery phase. |
| **G2: Acquire Meal** | Pick up one or more meals from the kitchen for the current order. | `-` (leaf) | Perform | AND (to AT1) | A single robot performs the pick‑up; no further decomposition is needed. |
| **G3: Deliver to Inpatient Room** | Execute the delivery step once the meal(s) have been acquired. | `;` | Perform | OR (fallback to G4a or G4b) | Two alternative delivery methods are available; either can satisfy the goal. |
| **G4a: Deliver via Manipulation** | Place the meal directly on the patient’s bedside table using a special manipulation skill. | `-` | Perform | AND (to AT2) | Requires a dedicated manipulation task; no other sub‑tasks are needed. |
| **G4b: Deliver via Tray Retrieval** | Hand the meal to the patient by letting them retrieve it from the robot’s tray. | `;` | Perform | AND (to G5–G9) | All these subtasks must be carried out in order: first assess capability, then perform retrieval, indicate which meal, record the event and alert if an error occurs. |
| **G5: Assess Retrieval Capability** | Query the patient’s record and the room’s companion status to determine whether the patient or a companion/nurse can retrieve the meal. | `-` | Query | AND (to AT3) | The information is obtained from a knowledge source; it is not an action performed by the robot. |
| **G6: Retrieve Meal from Tray with Cooperation** | Let the patient (or a companion/nurse/robot) pick up the meal from the robot’s tray. | `-` | Perform | AND (to AT4) | The task requires cooperation; the robot may work with one or two robots and a human. |
| **G7: Indicate Meal to Retrieve** | Tell the patient which specific meal they should take when multiple meals are carried. | `-` | Perform | AND (to AT5) | A simple verbal or visual cue delivered by the robot. |
| **G8: Track Retrieval Time & Location** | Log the moment and place where each meal was taken from the tray. | `-` | Perform | AND (to AT6) | The robot keeps an internal record of the event. |
| **G9: Alert Wrong Meal** | Warn the patient (or a nurse) if the wrong meal is taken from the tray. | `-` | Perform | AND (to AT7) | The robot must detect a mismatch between the indicated meal and the one actually retrieved. |
| **G10: Retrieve Dirty Dishes** | Collect all dirty plates/surfaces from the room. | `-` | Perform | AND (to AT8) | Dish retrieval may be done alone or with another robot; it is a separate sub‑task. |
| **G11: Open Door** | Unlock/ open the room door if it is closed, possibly with assistance from another robot or a human. | `-` | Perform | AND (to AT9) | The robot must ensure the door is accessible before entry. |
| **G12: Call Robot for Dishes** | Allow a patient or companion to request the robot to pick up dishes. | `-` | Perform | AND (to AT10) | This is an optional interaction that triggers dish retrieval. |

---

### Task Decomposition Tables

| **Name** | **Text** | **Relation** | **Location** | **Number of Robots** | **Justification** |
|----------|----------|--------------|--------------|-----------------------|-------------------|
| **AT1: Pick up Meal from Kitchen** | The robot physically lifts the meal(s) and places them in its tray. | AND (to G2) | Kitchen | 1 | Only one robot is required to load the meal; no cooperation needed. |
| **AT2: Deliver Meal to Room Table (Manipulation)** | The robot uses its manipulation arm to place the meal on the bedside table. | AND (to G4a) | Patient’s bedside table | 1 | The robot must be able to manipulate objects precisely; a single unit suffices. |
| **AT3: Assess Retrieval Capability** | The robot queries the patient record and checks for an accompanying nurse/visitor. | AND (to G5) | Internal database / patient record | 1 | Information is retrieved by the robot itself; no physical action. |
| **AT4: Retrieve Meal from Tray with Cooperation** | The robot offers the tray to the patient or a companion, allowing them to pick up the meal. | AND (to G6) | Patient’s bedside area | [1,2] | At least one robot must present the tray; if the patient can’t reach it alone, a second robot may help. |
| **AT5: Indicate Meal to Retrieve** | The robot verbally or visually indicates which meal the patient should take. | AND (to G7) | Patient’s bedside area | 1 | One robot can deliver the cue; no extra robots needed. |
| **AT6: Track Retrieval Time & Location** | The robot records the timestamp and the exact location of the meal retrieval event. | AND (to G8) | Internal system | 1 | The robot logs the data autonomously. |
| **AT7: Alert Wrong Meal** | If the retrieved meal does not match the indicated one, the robot raises an alarm. | AND (to G9) | Patient’s bedside area | 1 | A single robot can detect and signal the error. |
| **AT8: Retrieve Dirty Dishes** | The robot collects all dirty dishes from the room surface or tray. | AND (to G10) | Patient’s bedside area | [1,2] | Dish retrieval may be performed alone or with a second robot for efficiency. |
| **AT9: Open Door** | The robot unlocks and opens the patient’s door, potentially with human assistance. | AND (to G11) | Room door | [1,2] | One robot can handle the lock; if the door is stuck, a second robot or a human may help. |
| **AT10: Call Robot for Dishes** | The patient or companion signals the robot to fetch dishes; the robot then performs dish retrieval. | AND (to G12) | Patient’s bedside area | 1 | A single robot responds to the call and carries out the dish‑collection task. |

